| 2a | AT THE MERGE, ahead of rank 3 | the backup caps, so the Lararium holds every writer the backup repo takes (the keep's design at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep): `K1` `keep-cut` wakes each cold wiki in turn, hands the operator's pins back and refuses by name per (face, slug) on a shut face, so a page put into a cold wiki travels in the cut (`packages/lares-cli/src/rite-keep.ts`, `commands/rite.ts`, `tools/keep-cold.test.mjs`); `K2` the keep cuts house-only content, a workbench whose mirror rests beside the canon source staying out and the manifest naming it under `elsewhere` (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/house-bundle.ts`, `packages/lararium-node/src/bundle-manifest.ts`); `K1`, `K2` and `K11` stand BUILT: `K11` has the keep carry the device's AI-session state, `bin/sync`'s pieces living in `lares rite keep` (the device id, the one `~/.config/claude-backup/device.json` holds, and its refusal on a foreign `DEVICE.json`, the mirror of the `~/.claude` config, plugins, state and each project's `memory/`, the secret scan with its planted fixtures), all under `devices/<name>-<id8>/` in the same commit and the same push as `house/` (`packages/lares-cli/src/rite-keep-host.ts`, `keep-sessions.ts`, `keep-config.ts`); the sessions mirror and scan before any return spends, with the vessel down nothing commits, and `--no-sessions` or `LARES_KEEP_SESSIONS=0` keeps the house alone; the cadence covers `down`, an explicit `lares rite keep` and the SessionEnd hook `lares home tend` seats (`.claude-plugin/hooks/lares-keep-hook.mjs`, running `lares rite keep --if-due` detached), each push spending one return of the keep lei, which the operator sizes (the unlock offers twelve, and the wake names the count left); WAITING: `bin/sync` retires once one real sync reads par against a keep at the lit house, and the repo's README names a Lararium as its writer; the lit house's first keep pushed `par` (rank 4), and the comparison against `bin/sync` stays unwalked, held by no session's backlog | The re-bake's image carries whatever code stands at the re-bake, so with the caps in it the founded house's first `down` keeps the whole house and the device's sessions with no second image; every push into the backup repo rides a keep lei the operator strung, one writer per working tree, authority by capability and never by an ambient SSH key. |

